ITEM 2: ID TOP-UP / NEW CYCLE WORKFLOW (₹1,200 RE-ENTRY AFTER 126 MEMBERS)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Problem Reported:
  "After a cycle is completed at 126 members, the system must correctly show
   ₹1,200 TOP-UP REQUIRED – ACTIVATE NEW CYCLE on the Dashboard. This Top-Up alert
   must be RED in color with a blinking/pulsing effect, so it is clearly visible
   to the user. When I click it, it should open the ID Subscribe / Cycle Re-entry
   page. ₹1,200 must be deducted only from the Fund Wallet, and after successful
   backend confirmation, a new Cycle Number and Queue Position must be created.
   The new cycle must start from 0% with a new team structure. The previous
   cycle team and history must never be mixed with the new cycle."

* Root Cause:
  1. In backend/routes/cycles.routes.js (POST /activate), the backend had a hard check:
     `if (targetUser.status === 'ACTIVE') return res.status(400)...`
     When a user completed their first cycle of 126 members, targetUser.status was
     'ACTIVE', so the backend completely blocked them from re-entering or topping up.
  2. In mobile_app/lib/screens/navigation/home_screen.dart, the top-up alert was only
     checking `_membersCount >= 126`. When a cycle was marked COMPLETED, `activeCycle`
     became null and `_membersCount` fell back to 0, which immediately hid the alert.

* Fixation Done:
  1. In backend/routes/cycles.routes.js (POST /activate):
     - The backend now checks whether the user has an ONGOING active cycle (< 126 members).
     - If all previous cycles are COMPLETED (or members_count >= 126), the user is
       fully eligible for ₹1,200 Re-Entry / Top-Up.
     - Deducts ₹1,200 strictly from the payer's Fund Wallet (`fund_wallet_balance`).
     - Credits ₹300 Direct Sponsor Income to upline sponsor.
     - Logs ₹300 Company Maintenance.
     - Creates new sequential cycle row in `cycles` (`CYCLE-0002`, `CYCLE-0003`, etc.)
       with `status = 'ACTIVE'` and `members_count = 0`.
     - Places new cycle at the BOTTOM of `single_leg_queue`.
     - Previous cycle is dequeued from `single_leg_queue` and archived as completed history.
     - User's previous wallet earnings remain intact in Main Wallet and are never reset.
  2. In mobile_app/lib/screens/navigation/home_screen.dart:
     - Implemented dynamic blinking/pulsing RED alert card:
       * Title: "₹1,200 TOP-UP REQUIRED – ACTIVATE NEW CYCLE"
       * Subtitle: "Tap here to Top-Up ID (₹1,200) & unlock next cycle income!"
       * Color: Vivid Red (`Color(0xFFDC2626)`) with continuous pulsing opacity animation.
       * Trigger: Displays whenever `_isTopUpRequired || _membersCount >= 126 || (_cycleStatus == 'COMPLETED' && _activeCycleId.isEmpty)`.
       * Clicking opens id_subscription_screen.dart pre-filled for Cycle Re-entry.
  3. In mobile_app/lib/screens/recharge/id_subscription_screen.dart:
     - Allows re-entry if previous cycle is completed.
     - Changes action button to: "ACTIVATE NEW CYCLE (₹1,200)".

* Current Status:
  RESOLVED & VERIFIED. Re-entry creates a new Cycle ID at the bottom of the queue
  with 0% team, keeping history separated.

